          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For sprint and interval training, it is an excellent tool and the response is instant because there is no motor to spin up. For steady-state running it is worse than a motorised belt, since nothing enforces the pace and it drifts with your attention. It also needs no power at all, which suits a garage, but it is extremely heavy and does not move easily.",
          },
