        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long does a Woodway treadmill last?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Woodway publishes belt life figures in the tens of thousands of miles and the machines are designed to be rebuilt rather than replaced, which is why so many reach the used market still working after years of commercial service. We have not run one to destruction ourselves, so treat the published durability figures as the manufacturer's claims — but the secondhand market's existence is reasonable independent evidence.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
