          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between a slat belt and a normal treadmill belt?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A normal belt is one continuous rubber loop sliding across a fixed deck, and that sliding friction causes deck wear, rising motor load and the need for lubrication. A slat belt is many individual slats on a bearing system, so the surface rolls rather than slides. The result is firmer underfoot, more consistent over years, and free of the maintenance that friction creates.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
