          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Woodway solved the problem underneath almost every other treadmill problem: it removed the
            sliding friction. That buys <strong class="text-white">no lubrication, no deck wear and
            a machine designed to be rebuilt rather than replaced</strong> — and it costs what
            solving it properly costs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a facility, buy new. For a serious individual with a garage and a way to move 400 lbs,
            <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">buy used</a>
            — the secondhand market is unusually good here. For everyone else, this is a
            well-engineered answer to a problem you do not have, and
